165931113064289, 0.014416114427149296, 0.02619759552180767, -0.0019082494545727968, 0.014044291339814663, 0.020004084333777428, -0.03467516228556633, 0.023159269243478775, -0.03178556635975838, -0.007069951388984919, -0.0176350399851799, -0.03000081516802311, 0.02921467460691929, 0.06225381791591644, -0.02496526762843132, 0.0005062770214863122, -0.007473645266145468, 0.01058102399110794, 0.008875949308276176, 0.031551849097013474, 0.026792513206601143, 0.036757372319698334, -0.015605948865413666, -0.0246040690690279, -0.02577265538275242, -0.005959793925285339, -0.017666911706328392, 0.0026518958620727062, -0.011441529728472233, 0.032954152673482895, 0.021948188543319702, 0.011452152393758297, 0.024625316262245178]], "input": ["RESTRICCIÓN CALÓRICA:\"Restricción calórica\" is a dietary approach that involves reducing calorie intake, which may have significant effects on aging and health outcomes. This regimen has been shown to influence microbiota composition and obesity, suggesting that it plays a role in overall health and longevity.", "HOMBRE:HOMBRE es un género que se refiere a los varones humanos. En este contexto, se menciona en relación con el gasto energético basal, que es la cantidad mínima de energía que el cuerpo necesita para mantener sus funciones vitales en reposo.", "MUJER:The entity \"MUJER\" refers to a female individual, specifically in the context of energy expenditure, which is calculated using specific formulas. The term \"mujer\" also denotes the gender that pertains to human females, particularly in relation to basal energy expenditure. Additionally, women have increasingly participated in the labor market, which has influenced their food purchasing habits and the time allocated for food preparation. This multifaceted description highlights the biological, social, and economic aspects associated with women.", "GASTO ENERGÉTICO BASAL:Gasto energético basal (GEB) refers to the amount of energy expended by the body while at rest in a neutrally temperate environment and in the post-absorptive state. It represents the energy required to maintain vital functions while the body is not engaged in any physical activity. This expenditure is crucial for sustaining essential physiological processes, ensuring that the body can perform necessary functions even when at rest.", "GASTO ENERGÉTICO DIARIO:El gasto energético diario es la cantidad total de energía que una persona utiliza en un día, incluyendo actividad física y metabolismo basal.", "HIDRATOS DE CARBONO GLUCÉMICOS:Los hidratos de carbono glucémicos son aquellos que se convierten en glucosa y afectan los niveles de azúcar en sangre.", "HIDRATOS DE CARBONO NO GLICÉMICOS:Los hidratos de carbono no glicémicos, como la fibra, no se digieren y tienen un impacto diferente en la salud.", "AMERICAN HEART ASSOCIATION:The American Heart Association (AHA) is a prominent non-profit organization based in the United States dedicated to reducing the incidence of heart disease and stroke. Through a combination of education, research, and advocacy, the AHA aims to mitigate the impact of cardiovascular diseases on public health. The organization focuses on promoting cardiovascular health by publishing studies and guidelines that address various aspects of heart health, including dietary recommendations.\n\nThe AHA has conducted extensive research on dietary fats, specifically providing guidelines for fat intake to help prevent cardiovascular risks. It recommends that individuals limit their saturated fat intake to less than 7% of total daily calories and offers insights into the effects of dietary cholesterol on heart health. Additionally, the AHA has published studies regarding the consumption of omega-6 and omega-3 fatty acids, emphasizing their importance in a heart-healthy diet.\n\nOverall, the American Heart Association plays a crucial role in funding cardiovascular medical research and educating the public about healthy living practices to combat heart disease and stroke effectively.", "CÁNCER DE COLON:CÁNCER DE COLON, or colon cancer, is a type of cancer that can be influenced by various dietary factors. Research indicates that a diet rich in fiber, vitamin E, and vitamin C may play a significant role in the prevention of this disease. Specifically, an intake of 60 mg of vitamin C per day has been associated with a reduced risk of developing colon cancer, as highlighted by epidemiological studies. Additionally, the effects of omega-3 fatty acids on the development of colon cancer have also been a subject of research. Overall, colon cancer is a health risk that is closely linked to dietary intake, and it is a concern that is addressed in nutritional guidelines and recommendations.", "SENSIBILIDAD PERIFÉRICA A LA INSULINA:Peripheral insulin sensitivity is a metabolic condition that can be improved through dietary choices, particularly those high in fiber and complex carbohydrates.", "ASOCIACIÓN INTERNACIONAL PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LOS ÁCIDOS GRASOS Y LÍPIDOS:The \"ASOCIACIÓN INTERNACIONAL PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LOS ÁCIDOS GRASOS Y LÍPIDOS,\" also known as the International Society for the Study of Fatty Acids and Lipids (ISSFAL), is an international organization dedicated to providing guidance on the intake of fatty acids, particularly focusing on the essential fatty acids DHA (docosahexaenoic acid) and EPA (eicosapentaenoic acid). ISSFAL offers recommendations regarding the daily intake levels of these important nutrients, emphasizing their significance for health and nutrition.", "AGENCIA FRANCESA PARA LA SEGURIDAD SANITARIA DE LOS ALIMENTOS:The AGENCIA FRANCESA PARA LA SEGURIDAD SANITARIA DE LOS ALIMENTOS, known as AFSSA, is a French agency dedicated to ensuring food safety. It plays a crucial role in establishing dietary recommendations related to food safety, particularly focusing on the intake of fatty acids. Specifically, AFSSA provides guidelines for omega-3 fatty acids, emphasizing their importance in a balanced diet.", "FUNDACIÓN BRITÁNICA PARA LA NUTRICIÓN:The Fundación Británica para la Nutrición (BNF) is a British foundation dedicated to promoting healthy dietary practices. It offers comprehensive guidance on nutritional intake, including specific recommendations for fatty acid consumption. Among its key suggestions, the foundation emphasizes the importance of omega-3 fatty acids, providing evidence-based dietary guidelines to help individuals make informed choices about their nutrition.", "GRASAS SATURADAS:GRASAS SATURADAS, or saturated fats, are dietary fats that are associated with increased cardiovascular risk. Health recommendations advise limiting the intake of saturated fats to reduce this risk and improve overall health. Specifically, minimizing saturated fats in a healthy diet is suggested to enhance lipid profiles and decrease the likelihood of coronary disease.", "GRASAS HIDROGENADAS \"TRANS\":Trans fats are a type of unhealthy fat that can worsen lipid profiles and increase the risk of coronary disease.", "ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA:\"ENFERMEDAD CORONARIA,\" or coronary disease, is a medical condition characterized by the reduction of blood flow to the heart, primarily due to the buildup of plaque in the coronary arteries. This condition is often associated with obesity and metabolic health issues. Dietary factors play a significant role in the development and management of coronary disease, particularly the intake of dietary fats. The balance of omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids, as well as the consumption of alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) and fish rich in omega-3 fatty acids, can influence the risk of developing this condition. Overall, coronary disease is linked to various cardiovascular risk factors and can be mitigated through dietary choices."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}